---
title: CMN — Token Refresh Flow (Rotation)
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant FE as Frontend<br/>(@core/http interceptor)
    participant GW as Web Gateway
    participant AC as AuthController<br/>(POST /api/auth/refresh-login)
    participant AS as AuthAppService<br/>.RefreshLoginAsync
    participant JWT as JWT Parser
    participant R as Redis

    Note over FE: Triggered when any API call returns HTTP 401

    FE->>FE: Intercept 401 response
    FE->>FE: Read refreshToken from cookie REFRESH_TOKEN_KEY
    FE->>FE: Read expired accessToken from cookie ACCESS_TOKEN_KEY

    FE->>GW: POST /cmn/administration-service/api/auth/refresh-login<br/>Body: RefreshTokenInputDto { RefreshToken }<br/>Header: X-Tenant: {tenantId}<br/>[AllowAnonymous]
    GW->>AC: Forward
    AC->>AS: RefreshLoginAsync(input)

    Note over AS,JWT: Step 1 — Extract claims from expired token
    AS->>JWT: ParseExpiredToken(accessToken)
    JWT-->>AS: Claims: userId, sessionId

    Note over AS,R: Step 2 — Validate refresh token in Redis
    AS->>R: GET {userId}:{sessionId}
    R-->>AS: storedRefreshToken
    AS->>AS: Assert storedRefreshToken == input.RefreshToken

    Note over AS,R: Step 3 — Rotate: delete old, issue new
    AS->>R: DEL {userId}:{sessionId}
    AS->>AS: newSessionId = Guid.NewV7()
    AS->>AS: newAccessToken = CreateJWT(userId, newSessionId)<br/>Expiry=1h
    AS->>AS: newRefreshToken = "{UUIDv7}-{UUIDv7}"
    AS->>R: SET {userId}:{newSessionId} = newRefreshToken<br/>TTL 720h

    AS-->>AC: LoginOutputDto { AccessToken, RefreshToken, ... }
    AC-->>GW: 200 ApiResult<LoginOutputDto>
    GW-->>FE: 200

    FE->>FE: cookie.set(ACCESS_TOKEN_KEY, newAccessToken)
    FE->>FE: cookie.set(REFRESH_TOKEN_KEY, newRefreshToken)

    Note over FE: Retry original failed request with new token
    FE->>GW: Retry original request with new Authorization header
